+
+// A stricter variant of `extend_mode`, used only by callers that independently extend several
+// neighboring taps around a single sample point (e.g. `bicubic_sample`'s 16-tap kernel): doing
+// that can land a tap's raw position exactly on a wrap/reflection boundary far more often than
+// `extend_mode`'s original single-upfront-call usage ever did, which exposes two edge cases
+// `extend_mode` itself doesn't need to handle for its existing (single-tap) callers:
+//
+// - Repeat/Reflect's `max` is meant to be exclusive; the plain formula can still land exactly on
+//   it. Matches vello_cpu's `extend()`, which applies the identical `.min(max - 1.0)` safety
+//   clamp for this same reason (see its own comment "In certain edge cases, we might still end
+//   up with a higher number").
+// - Reflect additionally needs vello_cpu's exact 1-ULP-down bias in the "descending" (mirrored)
+//   half of the period (`vello_cpu/src/fine/common/image.rs`, itself sourced from
+//   <https://github.com/google/skia/blob/220738774f7a0ce4a6c7bd17519a336e5e5dea5b/src/opts/SkRasterPipeline_opts.h#L3274-L3290>)
+//   to avoid flooring to the texel just past the edge instead of the last real one when a tap's
+//   raw position lands exactly on the boundary.
+//
+// Deliberately not merged into `extend_mode` itself: `extend_mode`'s existing single-upfront-tap
+// callers (the un-fixed `bilinear_sample`/nearest-neighbor paths, and gradients via
+// `extend_mode_normalized` directly) already produce the correct result with the plain formula
+// for every case the project's own test suite exercises them with, and changing `extend_mode`'s
+// own Reflect output wholesale broke several of those (`image_bilinear_*_hybrid` tests) even
+// though they never call the new multi-tap code this variant exists for.
+fn extend_mode_precise(t: f32, mode: u32, max: f32) -> f32 {
+    switch mode {
+        case EXTEND_PAD: {
+            return clamp(t, 0.0, max - 1.0);
+        }
+        case EXTEND_REPEAT: {
+            return min(extend_mode_normalized(t / max, mode) * max, max - 1.0);
+        }
+        case EXTEND_REFLECT, default: {
+            let u = t - floor(t * 0.5 / max) * 2.0 * max;
+            let s = floor(u / max);
+            var m = u - 2.0 * s * (u - max);
+            let biased_bits = bitcast<u32>(m) - u32(s);
+            m = bitcast<f32>(biased_bits);
+            return min(m, max - 1.0);
+        }
+    }
+}
